author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "The merge resolution is recorded as a history entry whose patch reproduces the merged item state exactly, so the last after_hash equals the hash of the merged item file and pm history --verify passes with no manual step; The entry carries merge provenance: the contributing stream heads or branch identities, the driver that produced the resolution, and per-field attribution for any field where the branches disagreed; pm restore and pm get --at can address the merged state like any other version, asserted by a test that merges divergent branches and then restores to the post-merge version from the stream alone; A clean merge leaves pm validate with zero history-drift warnings, and a genuine tamper still fails, so the drift signal keeps its meaning; history-repair keeps declining to rewrite a verifying chain: recording the resolution is the fix, and repair is not extended to fabricate entries; Recording is deterministic and order-independent, so merging the same branch set in different orders yields the same merged state and equivalent recorded provenance; The workspace-scope equivalent is covered or explicitly deferred with a reason: settings, schema, and relationship artifacts merged by the same fence get the same treatment"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: high
confidence: 75
